# Use shadcn/ui

When building or changing UI in this repo:

- Prefer components from `src/components/ui/` (shadcn). Do not hand-roll buttons, inputs, selects, dialogs, calendars, popovers, or date pickers when a shadcn primitive exists or can be added.
- Add missing primitives with `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <name>` (respect `components.json`, style `base-nova`).
- Compose patterns the shadcn way (e.g. Date Picker = `Popover` + `Calendar` via `@/components/ui/date-picker`).
- Do not use raw `<input type="date">`, custom modal overlays, or one-off CSS control kits for standard controls.
- Keep Vietnamese labels; match existing Button/Input/Select APIs (`render` prop where Base UI requires it).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<input type="date" value={iso} onChange={...} />

// ✅ GOOD
import { DatePicker } from "@/components/ui/date-picker"
<DatePicker value={iso} onChange={setIso} min={boundsMin} max={boundsMax} />
```

Follow skill `use-shadcn` for the full checklist.
